WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:05.500 --> 00:00:07.080
Under the United States Constitution,

00:00:07.080 --> 00:00:08.639
Congress makes the laws and the

00:00:08.639 --> 00:00:10.530
president enforces the laws. The law

00:00:10.530 --> 00:00:12.809
provides authority for the president and

00:00:12.809 --> 00:00:14.700
the agencies of the government to compel

00:00:14.700 --> 00:00:17.220
individuals, corporations, and others to

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.949
take - or not to take - certain acts. For

00:00:19.949 --> 00:00:21.630
example, a law authorizes the

00:00:21.630 --> 00:00:23.730
president to collect taxes through the

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:25.590
Internal Revenue Service. Neither the

00:00:25.590 --> 00:00:28.199
president nor the IRS can collect taxes,

00:00:28.199 --> 00:00:30.840
or do anything else, without a supporting

00:00:30.840 --> 00:00:31.949
law from Congress.

00:00:31.949 --> 00:00:34.170
However, the laws leave the IRS and other

00:00:34.170 --> 00:00:36.600
agencies with discretion on HOW they

00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:38.850
enforce the law. An executive order is

00:00:38.850 --> 00:00:40.620
the president's written direction to the

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:42.719
agencies of the government about how he

00:00:42.719 --> 00:00:45.149
wants them to act when they enforce the

00:00:45.149 --> 00:00:47.579
law. For example, President Trump issued

00:00:47.579 --> 00:00:49.620
an executive order directing all

00:00:49.620 --> 00:00:52.440
agencies to eliminate two regulations for

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:54.870
every regulation they issue. As long as the

00:00:54.870 --> 00:00:56.070
order is consistent with the

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:57.930
Constitution and the law, the president

00:00:57.930 --> 00:01:00.629
can use an executive order to tell the

00:01:00.629 --> 00:01:03.539
IRS and others HOW he wants them to do

00:01:03.539 --> 00:01:06.519
what Congress has authorized.

00:01:07.409 --> 00:01:10.799
Are executive orders by President Trump a good idea?

00:01:10.799 --> 00:01:12.540
Let us know in your comments, and also

00:01:12.540 --> 00:01:14.640
let us know what other topics you want

00:01:14.640 --> 00:01:22.490
AEI scholars to cover in 60 seconds.

